model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "App managers control generic, per-app tool availability independently of approval rules. Availability only narrows existing grants; it filters discovery before pagination and search ranking, and is rechecked on calls, nested app operations and resumed approvals. The trusted SDK runtime checks availability before dispatch, including workflow steps in retained bundles without policy callbacks. Agent management uses the built-in management app's ordinary approval flow. Hosted migration 18 adds state without rewriting existing tables; retained-data fixtures remove its table and journal row before replaying older migrations. Warm MCP calls reuse availability from their access snapshot without extra statements or writes; nested invocations and discarded batches read live. Linked-account changes invalidate manager catalogs. Managers can reveal hidden inventory and restore tools."
    }
  }
}
